{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 109, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 1->3 absent, edge 5 is one of the few routes into the output, so putting a conv there adds much-needed capacity (cf. exp 60)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 2->3 is removed, edge 1->3 carries more of the output signal, so a conv there matters more."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 1->3 missing, the direct 0->3 edge is a main output path and turning it into a conv gives large gains (cf. exps 83, 89)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 1->3 when edge 2->3 is already gone can leave the output with only the 0->3 edge, which can collapse accuracy (cf. exp 82)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 2->3 when edge 1->3 is absent removes all deep paths into the output, leaving only the shallow 0->3 edge."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the first edge with a conv adds capacity, while replacing another op gains little or nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the conv on edge 2->3 for an identity throws away learned features, whereas replacing pooling or none with skip usually helps."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling with a 3x3 conv on edge 1->3 gives the largest capacity gain (cf. exp 38), larger than replacing skip or a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 1->3 is absent, turning the direct 0->3 edge into pooling further weakens an already thin set of output paths (cf. exp 48)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1->2 removed, node 2 is fed only by edge 0->2, so making it a pooling op starves the 2->3 path of learned features (cf. exp 79)."}], "tok": 16842, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [2, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect"], [1, "none"]], [["none", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect"], [2, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect"], [2, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "skip_connect"], [2, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["av